"help.title"      = "How this works";
"help.saturation" = "Saturation rewrites the display's colour profile so macOS sends more vivid signals to a panel with a narrow gamut.";
"help.video"      = "Video Enhance brightens only the darkest part of the image and leaves mid-tones and highlights exactly as they were. Colour e-ink has a low contrast ratio, so dark detail collapses into an undifferentiated mush; this spreads those tones apart so they become visible.";
"help.tradeoff"   = "The trade-off: it cannot tell dark video from dark text. Anything dark gets lighter, so body text loses contrast — noticeably so in Dark Mode, where the background lifts too. That is why it is recommended for video and photos, and off while reading.";
"help.volatile"   = "Both adjustments need this app running: quitting restores every display to its original state, and launching puts your settings back.";

